---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  TooltipBrands,
  TooltipColumnHints,
  TooltipComposer,
  TooltipPlayground,
  TooltipSidebar,
} from "../../components/TooltipDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Tooltip"
  description="Short labels for icon buttons, column hints, and collapsed navigation."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Tooltip</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A short label that appears when a control is hovered or focused. Use it to
    name icon buttons, explain a column, or show a shortcut. Keep the text to
    one line or two; anything longer belongs in a popover.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="tooltip-demo"><TooltipPlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Tooltip usage"
      code={`import { Paperclip } from "reicon-react/icons/Paperclip";
import { Button } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/button";
import {
  Tooltip,
  TooltipContent,
  TooltipProvider,
  TooltipTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/tooltip";

<TooltipProvider>
  <Tooltip>
    <TooltipTrigger
      render={<Button size="icon-sm" variant="ghost" aria-label="Attach files" />}
    >
      <Paperclip size={16} aria-hidden="true" />
    </TooltipTrigger>
    <TooltipContent>Attach files from your device</TooltipContent>
  </Tooltip>
</TooltipProvider>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass the control to <code>TooltipTrigger</code> through <code>render</code
      >. Icon-only triggers still need an <code>aria-label</code>; the tooltip
      describes the control, it doesn’t name it. Wrap a toolbar, header row, or
      whole app in one <code>TooltipProvider</code> so moving between neighbours opens
      each tooltip straight away.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Composer toolbar</h2>
    <p>
      Ghost <code>icon-sm</code> and <code>sm</code> buttons, a select trigger, and
      a popover trigger can all be tooltip triggers. To combine triggers, nest them:
      <code
        >{
          "<TooltipTrigger render={<PopoverTrigger render={<Button />} />} />"
        }</code
      >. The send button switches between <code>default</code> and <code
        >secondary</code
      > and is disabled while the draft is empty; a disabled button can’t be hovered
      or focused, so its tooltip stays closed. While a reply is sending, a stop button
      takes its place.
    </p>
    <TooltipComposer client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Column hints</h2>
    <p>
      A plain <code>button</code> with an info icon explains a column heading. Long
      hints wrap at 20rem.
    </p>
    <TooltipColumnHints client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">App tiles</h2>
    <p>
      <code>BrandStack</code> gives every tile a tooltip with the app’s name. Render
      a <code>BrandTile</code> as the trigger for a single tile.
    </p>
    <TooltipBrands client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Collapsed sidebar</h2>
    <p>
      <code>SidebarMenuButton</code> takes a <code>tooltip</code> string or an object
      of <code>TooltipContent</code> props. It shows beside the icon rail only while
      the sidebar is collapsed; pass <code>hidden</code> in the object to override
      that. It works on links, on plain buttons with <code
        >aria-keyshortcuts</code
      >, and as the <code>render</code> target of a <code
        >DropdownMenuTrigger</code
      >.
    </p>
    <TooltipSidebar client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="tooltip-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>TooltipProvider</code> takes the Base UI provider props <code
        >delay</code
      > (0 here), <code>closeDelay</code>, and <code>timeout</code>. A tooltip
      outside a provider waits 600ms.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>Tooltip</code> and <code>TooltipTrigger</code> wrap the Base UI tooltip
      root and trigger and take their props, including <code>open</code>, <code
        >defaultOpen</code
      >, <code>onOpenChange</code>, <code>disabled</code>, <code>delay</code>, <code
        >closeOnClick</code
      >, and <code>render</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>TooltipContent</code> renders its own portal, positioner, and arrow. It
      takes <code>side</code> (<code>"top"</code>), <code>align</code> (<code
        >"center"</code
      >), <code>sideOffset</code> (4), <code>alignOffset</code> (0), <code
        >collisionPadding</code
      > (8), <code>anchor</code>, <code>keepMounted</code>, <code
        >container</code
      >, <code>hidden</code>, and every Base UI popup prop. Each part sets a <code
        >data-slot</code
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Tooltips open on hover and on keyboard focus, and close on Escape, blur,
      or pointer leave. While one is showing it has <code>role="tooltip"</code>
      and the trigger’s <code>aria-describedby</code> points at it, merged with any
      description the trigger already has. Never put links or buttons in a tooltip;
      it can’t receive focus.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tooltips fade and scale in from their side over 120ms, and open instantly
      when moving between neighbours in a provider. Motion turns off when
      reduced motion is requested. In forced-colors mode the label and arrow
      keep a visible border.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Tooltips use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code
        >--sprout-text</code
      >, <code>--sprout-shadow-panel</code>, the control radius, and the extra
      small text size. They need no brand color, so they look the same with the
      neutral and TulipFarm themes in light and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
